WEBVTT

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.240
(ORCHESTRAL MUSIC PLAYING)

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.400
(CHORUS CHANTING YOIK)

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.040
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.880
AGNARR: Anna. Elsa.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.240
IDUNA: Bedtime soon.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.240
Uh-oh. The princess is trapped

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:03.840
in the snow goblin's
evil spell.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.640
Quick, Elsa! Make a prince!
A fancy one!

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.880
Oh, no!
The prince is trapped, too.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.520
(IN DEEP VOICE)
Who cares about danger

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.680
when there's love?

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.400
-(MIMICS KISSING)
-Ugh, Anna. Bleugh!

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.480
Kissing won't save the Forest.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.880
-(YOUNG ANNA GIGGLES)
-The lost fairies cry out.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.240
(MIMICS TRUMPETING)

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.400
What sound
does a giraffe make?

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.520
-(MUMBLES)
-Never mind.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.800
They wake the fairy queen...

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.640
who breaks the spell
and saves everyone!

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.600
-And they all get married!
-(GIGGLES)

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.080
What are you playing?

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.720
Enchanted Forest.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.080
The prince and the princess...

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.560
Hmm. That's like no enchanted
forest I've ever seen.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.560
(GASPS) You've seen
an enchanted forest?

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.640
Wait, what?

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.720
I have. Once.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:43.360
And you've never
told us this before?

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.480
Well, I could tell you now,
if you...

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.960
(GIRLS GIGGLING)

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.640
-Okay. Now.
-Tell us now.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.280
Are you sure about this?

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.720
It's time they know.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.440
(WHISPERS) Let's make
a big snowman later.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.040
If they can settle and listen.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.640
(BOTH HOLDING BREATH)

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:58.960
(CHUCKLES)

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.200
Far away...

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.200
as north as we can go...

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.000
stood a very old
and very enchanted forest.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.960
But its magic wasn't that of

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.400
goblin spells
and lost fairies.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.800
It was protected by the most
powerful spirits of all...

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.040
those of air...

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:17.720
of fire...

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.000
of water...

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.520
and earth.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.960
But it was also home

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.960
to the mysterious
Northuldra people.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.760
YOUNG ELSA: Were the
Northuldra magical, like me?

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.480
AGNARR: No, Elsa.
They were not magical.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.880
They just took advantage
of the Forest's gifts.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.720
Their ways
were so different from ours...

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.440
but still,
they promised us friendship.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.400
In honor of that,

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.360
your grandfather,
King Runeard,

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.840
built them a mighty dam...

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.600
to strengthen their waters.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.360
It was a gift of peace.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.480
YOUNG ANNA:
That's a big gift of peace.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.360
AGNARR: And I was so honored

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.320
to get to go to the Forest
to celebrate it.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:02.680
RUNEARD: Stand tall, Agnarr.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.120
AGNARR:
I wasn't at all prepared

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.520
for what the day would bring.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.800
(CROWD CHATTERING EXCITEDLY)

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.840
We let down our guard.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:12.680
(LAUGHS)

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.200
We were charmed.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:15.840
Whoa. Whoa!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:16.960
(CHUCKLES)

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.040
It felt so...

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.200
magical.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.960
-(CHITTERING)
-(GASPS)

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.400
(GIGGLING)

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.560
-But something went wrong.
-(MAN YELLS)

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.400
(ALL GRUNTING)

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.160
They were attacking us.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.040
Get behind me.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.440
AGNARR:
It was a brutal battle.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.000
-Your grandfather...
-(RUNEARD YELPS)

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.160
Father!

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.240
AGNARR: ...was lost.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.360
Aah!

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.440
AGNARR: The fighting
enraged the spirits.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.600
FIGHTER: Look out!

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.840
AGNARR: They turned
their magic against us all.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.160
(YELPS, GRUNTS)

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.800
(ANGELIC VOICE VOCALIZING)

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.200
There was this voice...

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:13.840
(WIND GUSTING)

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.360
...and someone saved me.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:23.680
I'm told
the spirits then vanished.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:27.920
And a powerful mist
covered the Forest.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.360
Locking everyone out.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.840
(WIND WHISTLING)

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:39.520
And that night, I came home
King of Arendelle.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.040
Whoa, Papa, that was epic.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.280
Whoever saved you,

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.440
-I love them.
-(AGNARR CHUCKLES)

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.360
I wish I knew who it was.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.560
What happened to the spirits?

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.040
What's in the Forest now?

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.760
I don't know.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.240
The mist still stands.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.160
No one can get in.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.040
And no one has since come out.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.400
So we're safe.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.560
Yes.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.600
But the Forest
could wake again.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.600
And we must be prepared for
whatever danger it may bring.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.040
IDUNA: And on that note,

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.600
how about we say good night
to your father?

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:18.160
(WHINES) But I still have
so many questions.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:20.120
Save them
for another night, Anna.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:23.000
(SIGHS) You know I don't have
that kind of patience.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.080
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.960
Why did Northuldra
attack us anyway?

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.040
Who attacks people
who give them gifts?

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.920
Do you think
the Forest will wake again?

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.200
Only Ahtohallan knows.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.200
Octa-who-what?

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:40.200
(GASPS SOFTLY)

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.320
(SIGHS) When I was little...

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.040
my mother would sing a song

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.640
about a special river
called Ahtohallan...

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.680
that was said to hold all
the answers about the past.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.880
About what we are a part of.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.040
Wow.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.160
Will you sing it for us?
Please?

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.800
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:57.920
Okay.

00:05:58.080 --> 00:05:59.920
-Cuddle close.
-(YOUNG ANNA GIGGLES)

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.200
-Scooch in.
-(YOUNG ELSA GIGGLES)

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.560
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.920
(SINGING) Where the Northwind

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.200
Meets the sea

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.320
There's a river

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:17.400
Full of memory

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:22.480
Sleep, my darling,
safe and sound

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:27.320
For in this river,
all is found

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:29.920
(SNORING)

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:33.320
In her waters

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.240
Deep and true

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.400
Lie the answers

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.040
And a path for you

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:46.240
Dive down deep into her sound

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:51.760
But not too far
or you'll be drowned

